# Two-button navigation (Tawni common map)

Read `../../TAWNI_RULES.md` section **3a**. That shared shell **wins**. Do not invent new SoftAP / soft-off / wake timings.

## Physical (never swap, including Flip 180)

| Marking | GPIO | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bottom / setup mark | **GPIO0** | Primary / setup |
| Top | **GPIO28** | Secondary |

## Shared on every firmware

| Input | Action | Timing |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bottom long alone (GPIO0) | SoftAP on/off (SSID `TawniWardriver`) | ~2 s |
| Both held | Soft power-off | ~3 s |
| Bottom after wake (GPIO0) | Stay awake | ~1.5 s |

Dual-hold must suppress SoftAP long-press. Soft-off blocked during OTA. GPIO0 alone leaves SoftAP while AP is up. Settings stay on SoftAP - no nested cabin menus.

## This firmware's short / top-long jobs

| Input | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Bottom short (GPIO0) | Start / stop logging |
| Top short (GPIO28) | Next page |
| Top long (GPIO28) | Previous page |

When adding features: keep the shared rows identical; only change short-press / top-long if it still fits two buttons.